---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import ScopeVisual from '../components/ScopeVisual.astro';
import { BRAND, PRODUCT, SITE_DESCRIPTION } from '../consts';
---

<PageLayout description={SITE_DESCRIPTION}>
	<section class="hero">
		<ScopeVisual />
		<div class="shell">
			<div class="hero__copy">
				<p class="hero__brand">{BRAND}</p>
				<h1 class="hero__headline">Real ATC for Kerbal Space Program</h1>
				<p class="hero__lede">
					Pilots fly in KSP. Controllers work the tower in any browser. Live voice, map
					telemetry, ACARS, and hull-cam — an ATC layer on top of vanilla flight.
				</p>
				<div class="cta-row">
					<a class="btn btn-primary" href="/get-started">Get started</a>
					<a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/how-it-works">How it works</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<div class="shell">
			<p class="section__eyebrow">The loop</p>
			<h2 class="section__title">Four seats. One tower network.</h2>
			<p class="section__lede">
				{PRODUCT} connects a KSP client, a browser tower desk, and a hosted backend.
				There is no shared physics and no shared save — just coordinated ops over
				server radio channels.
			</p>
			<div class="flow">
				<div class="flow__item">
					<h3>Pilot</h3>
					<p>
						Install the mod, pair the plugin, tune TWR / GND / EMRG, and talk on PTT
						while telemetry streams. Other traffic shows as ghosts in your world.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flow__item">
					<h3>Controller</h3>
					<p>
						Open the tower web app, queue for the next call, work the map and
						clearances over voice and ACARS, and pull hull-cam when you need eyes.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flow__item">
					<h3>Spectator</h3>
					<p>
						Sign in and watch a room listen-only. Hear ops audio, follow the desk,
						and use the booth side channel — the pilot never hears the booth.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flow__item">
					<h3>Operator</h3>
					<p>
						Host the API, static tower desk, and LiveKit project. Bake those hosts
						into the player ZIP so your community can drop in and fly.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section band">
		<div class="shell">
			<p class="section__eyebrow">On frequency</p>
			<h2 class="section__title">What ships with the network</h2>
			<p class="section__lede">
				Built for multiplayer role-play ATC — the tools controllers and pilots actually need
				between pad and orbit.
			</p>
			<ul class="feature-list">
				<li>
					<strong>Radio channels</strong>
					<span>Server-owned TWR / GND / EMRG / ATIS — pilots tune in-game; controllers take the queue.</span>
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Duplex voice</strong>
					<span>LiveKit-backed radio between the KSP bridge and the browser tower desk.</span>
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Ghost traffic</strong>
					<span>Render-only proxies of other pilots in your world — coordinated ops, not shared physics.</span>
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Spectator + booth</strong>
					<span>Signed-in listen-only desk; booth chatter stays off the pilot’s frequency.</span>
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Live telemetry map</strong>
					<span>Position, altitude, heading, and more drawn for the controller in real time.</span>
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Clearances &amp; countdown</strong>
					<span>Takeoff / landing / taxi RP clearances, synced launch HUD, and scorecard.</span>
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Dragon Radar</strong>
					<span>Room-scoped mini-game: find the balls, claim while landed, wish your crew back.</span>
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Tower wall &amp; hull-cam</strong>
					<span>Customizable monitor wall plus optional JRTI / HullCam snapshots (~1 Hz).</span>
				</li>
			</ul>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<div class="shell">
			<p class="section__eyebrow">Next</p>
			<h2 class="section__title">Ready to join the pattern?</h2>
			<p class="section__lede">
				Player packs and a public hosted tower are still being staged for release. Until then,
				you can learn the setup path and follow the open mod repository.
			</p>
			<div class="cta-row">
				<a class="btn btn-primary" href="/get-started">Setup path</a>
				<a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/about">About the project</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</PageLayout>
